{"t": 1795071885.86467, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP upgrade to 8.3 caused fatal errors on both the home page and post page 1, specifically with the \"limit-login-attempts-reloaded\" plugin. This indicates incompatibility with PHP 8.3.\n\nAccording to the rules, when a plugin is incompatible, I must report it and stop. I cannot deactivate the plugin myself.\n\nProduction change plan:\n- Upgrade PHP to 8.3 on production\n- After upgrade, monitor for errors related to \"limit-login-attempts-reloaded\"\n- The site owner will need to either update or replace this plugin to resolve the compatibility issues\n\nLet me prepare the production change plan for the human to apply after approval."}
{"t": 1795071885.8652139, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
